{Greco recorded this line four hundred years ago. It is the Greek gift in its purest form: every attacking piece arrives with tempo.}
1. e4 e6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Bd3 Nc6 4. Nf3 Bb4+ 5. c3 Ba5 6. h4 {Already planning the sacrifice: the h-pawn will support a knight on g5 and later open the h-file.} O-O 7. e5 Nd5 {The knight is driven from f6, the one piece that guards h7. Now every condition on the checklist is met.} 8. Bxh7+ {The gift.} Kxh7 9. Ng5+ Kg8 {The most natural retreat, and the losing one.} 10. Qh5 {Threatening Qh7 mate. Black can only delay it.} Re8 {Making room for the king on f8.} 11. Qxf7+ Kh8 12. Qh5+ Kg8 13. Qh7+ Kf8 14. Qh8+ Ke7 15. Qxg7# 1-0
